704
00:32:41,640 --> 00:32:42,810
Here's selection.

705
00:32:42,810 --> 00:32:46,310
Selection is nested
for loops also.

706
00:32:46,310 --> 00:32:50,450
So here's, again,
selection-- basically,

707
00:32:50,450 --> 00:32:53,720
if you're sorting
these by ascending,

708
00:32:53,720 --> 00:32:57,280
it goes through and selects
the smallest number,

709
00:32:57,280 --> 00:33:00,950
swaps it with the first spot and
it moves on to the second spot.

710
00:33:00,950 --> 00:33:05,990
It goes through and it finds a
next smallest number, swaps it.

711
00:33:05,990 --> 00:33:07,540
It selects-- selection sort.

712
00:33:07,540 --> 00:33:11,650
It selects the smallest number,
swaps it with that spot,

713
00:33:11,650 --> 00:33:14,500
selects the next smallest
number, swaps it.

714
00:33:14,500 --> 00:33:20,010
The insertion sort,
the insertion sort

715
00:33:20,010 --> 00:33:23,660
treats the list like
two separate lists.

716
00:33:23,660 --> 00:33:28,800
It starts with the sorted
list and an unsorted list.

717
00:33:28,800 --> 00:33:32,070
And the sorted list starts
out with just one item.

718
00:33:32,070 --> 00:33:36,480
So this list of three
right here is sorted.

719
00:33:36,480 --> 00:33:37,840
It's got one thing in it.

720
00:33:37,840 --> 00:33:40,080
Then it goes and it
grabs the next item,

721
00:33:40,080 --> 00:33:42,660
and it inserts it
into the sorted list

722
00:33:42,660 --> 00:33:45,040
into the correct spot.

723
00:33:45,040 --> 00:33:45,720
So it'll be 1-3.

724
00:33:45,720 --> 00:33:46,480
Three.

725
00:33:46,480 --> 00:33:49,758
Then it'll grab the 4 and
insert it into the sorted list,

726
00:33:49,758 --> 00:33:50,800
and it'll leave it there.

727
00:33:50,800 --> 00:33:51,970
It'll be 1-3-4.

728
00:33:51,970 --> 00:33:53,580
Then it'll grab
the next number 1.

729
00:33:53,580 --> 00:33:55,660
It'll insert it into
the sorted list.

730
00:33:55,660 --> 00:33:57,060
It'll be 1-1-3-4.

731
00:33:57,060 --> 00:33:58,560
And it keeps going.

732
00:33:58,560 --> 00:33:59,880
That's insertion sort.

733
00:33:59,880 --> 00:34:02,370
It keeps a sorted list
and an unsorted list,

734
00:34:02,370 --> 00:34:07,720
and it inserts values one at a
time into these sorted lists.

735
00:34:07,720 --> 00:34:12,699
What is the order of complexity
of the insertion sort?

736
00:34:12,699 --> 00:34:13,710
N squared.

