00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:28,810
ANDREW BRIM: Educated
guess is correct.

743
00:34:28,810 --> 00:34:32,752
So if the insertion
sort is already sorted,

744
00:34:32,752 --> 00:34:34,210
you can add-- this
doesn't have it.

745
00:34:34,210 --> 00:34:39,540
You can add an if statement to
say, if the number I'm inserting

746
00:34:39,540 --> 00:34:43,739
is greater than the largest
number in the sorted array,

747
00:34:43,739 --> 00:34:45,719
I can leave it alone.

748
00:34:45,719 --> 00:34:47,550
So instead of doing
a nested for loop,

749
00:34:47,550 --> 00:34:50,880
you can just do an if statement
for each one of these,

750
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:54,120
and it's an order n operation.

751
00:34:54,120 --> 00:34:59,490
So that's why insertion sort
was preferred for a long time.

