1348
01:04:28,940 --> 01:04:33,140
Remember, inorder traversal
is you go left, print,

1349
01:04:33,140 --> 01:04:36,090
go right, OK?

1350
01:04:36,090 --> 01:04:37,290
So we go left printing.

1351
01:04:37,290 --> 01:04:41,340
So the first thing you'll always
print in inorder is the min.

1352
01:04:41,340 --> 01:04:47,320
So we go left, go left A, go
back up, print plus, go right.

1353
01:04:47,320 --> 01:04:50,560
Do we print the star,
the multiply yet?

1354
01:04:50,560 --> 01:04:51,060
No.

1355
01:04:51,060 --> 01:04:53,800
Go left, print B, then come up.

1356
01:04:53,800 --> 01:04:55,270
Then print the multiply.

1357
01:04:55,270 --> 01:04:56,560
Go right.

1358
01:04:56,560 --> 01:04:59,580
C is children are null,
null, so we print c.

1359
01:04:59,580 --> 01:05:05,040
Then we return, return, return,
and now we print the root.

1360
01:05:05,040 --> 01:05:09,650
So what character is the root
going to get printed here?

1361
01:05:09,650 --> 01:05:11,580
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6.

1362
01:05:11,580 --> 01:05:13,500
6, the root will get printed.

1363
01:05:13,500 --> 01:05:17,020
Then we do the same
thing to the right.

1364
01:05:17,020 --> 01:05:18,743
We print-- or, you
guys tell me, what's

1365
01:05:18,743 --> 01:05:20,160
the-- when I go
right here, what's

1366
01:05:20,160 --> 01:05:21,618
the first thing
I'm going to print?

1367
01:05:21,618 --> 01:05:22,140
STUDENT: D.

1368
01:05:22,140 --> 01:05:23,015
ANDREW BRIM: D, good.

1369
01:05:23,015 --> 01:05:31,840
So D times E plus F
times G. You got it.

1370
01:05:31,840 --> 01:05:32,780
Good, all right.

1371
01:05:32,780 --> 01:05:35,620
How about preorder traversal?

1372
01:05:35,620 --> 01:05:39,070
Preorder, remember, we
print first, then we go.

1373
01:05:39,070 --> 01:05:42,060
So we go plus, yep, plus--

1374
01:05:42,060 --> 01:05:43,240
STUDENT: A.

1375
01:05:43,240 --> 01:05:48,700
ANDREW BRIM: A, times B,
C, back, back, back, back,

1376
01:05:48,700 --> 01:05:57,380
times plus, times D,
E, F, G. You got it?

1377
01:05:57,380 --> 01:05:57,970
Really fast.

1378
01:05:57,970 --> 01:05:58,730
We'll do it again slower?

1379
01:05:58,730 --> 01:05:59,840
Let's do it again slower.

1380
01:05:59,840 --> 01:06:02,870
Remember, you print first.

1381
01:06:02,870 --> 01:06:06,600
So we print plus first, go left.

1382
01:06:06,600 --> 01:06:09,720
Print plus first, go left.

1383
01:06:09,720 --> 01:06:12,320
Print A first, go
left, go right.

1384
01:06:12,320 --> 01:06:14,220
They're nulls.

1385
01:06:14,220 --> 01:06:15,140
Return.

1386
01:06:15,140 --> 01:06:17,800
Now we go-- we've
already gone left.

1387
01:06:17,800 --> 01:06:19,740
You guys with me on,
we're going right next?

1388
01:06:19,740 --> 01:06:21,720
STUDENT: So we have 2
plus n is [INAUDIBLE]?

1389
01:06:21,720 --> 01:06:23,520
ANDREW BRIM: Yeah, exactly.

1390
01:06:23,520 --> 01:06:26,610
2 plus n ends in a, is what
Lucy said for those on Zoom.

1391
01:06:26,610 --> 01:06:28,140
Then we go right.

1392
01:06:28,140 --> 01:06:29,130
We get to a plus.

1393
01:06:29,130 --> 01:06:29,920
What do we do?

1394
01:06:29,920 --> 01:06:30,210
STUDENT: [INAUDIBLE]

1395
01:06:30,210 --> 01:06:31,127
ANDREW BRIM: Preorder.

1396
01:06:31,127 --> 01:06:33,100
We print it-- yep,
print the times.

1397
01:06:33,100 --> 01:06:35,770
Then we go left,
print b, return.

1398
01:06:35,770 --> 01:06:37,690
Then we go right,
print c, return.

1399
01:06:37,690 --> 01:06:40,717
Now I'm coming all the way
back up, return, return,

1400
01:06:40,717 --> 01:06:41,550
and I'm at the root.

1401
01:06:41,550 --> 01:06:43,790
Do I print the root now?

1402
01:06:43,790 --> 01:06:46,000
No, we already printed it--
preorder traversal, OK?

1403
01:06:46,000 --> 01:06:49,450
And then we do the same
thing on the right subtree.

1404
01:06:49,450 --> 01:06:52,220
Print the times, go left.

1405
01:06:52,220 --> 01:06:54,890
Print the plus, go left.

1406
01:06:54,890 --> 01:06:57,440
Print the times, go left.

1407
01:06:57,440 --> 01:06:59,900
Print the D, children
are both null.

1408
01:06:59,900 --> 01:07:01,280
Return, go right.

1409
01:07:01,280 --> 01:07:03,230
Print the E, children
are both null.

1410
01:07:03,230 --> 01:07:03,940
Return.

1411
01:07:03,940 --> 01:07:05,180
Return to the plus.

1412
01:07:05,180 --> 01:07:06,350
Go right.

1413
01:07:06,350 --> 01:07:08,330
Print the F. Children
are both null.

1414
01:07:08,330 --> 01:07:09,190
Return.

1415
01:07:09,190 --> 01:07:11,150
Return, we've
already printed this.

1416
01:07:11,150 --> 01:07:11,870
Go right.

1417
01:07:11,870 --> 01:07:13,880
Print the G. Children
are both null.

1418
01:07:13,880 --> 01:07:16,900
Return, return-- preorder.

1419
01:07:20,230 --> 01:07:21,880
Postorder.

1420
01:07:21,880 --> 01:07:24,730
What's the last thing we're
going to print in a postorder

1421
01:07:24,730 --> 01:07:25,280
